A shortcut, not Palm's app.

Palm's Wi-Fi app talks to webOS's own wifi service and manages the device's radio. Lunacy
doesn't own the radio - Android does - so a copy of that UI here could only pretend. This app
is an icon that opens Android's Wi-Fi settings instead (appinfo.json's lunacyAndroidSettings,
a Lunacy extension), and it holds no code of its own.

icon.png and icon-256x256.png are Palm's, from com.palm.app.wifi as shipped on webOS 3.x, so
the icon looks like the one webOS users know. Copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-Packard; never
released under an open licence; distributed by Lunacy as abandonware, like Mojo and the
Prelude fonts.
